WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´ve been such a fan of yours
for so long.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this year --
just a fantastic year.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.641
"The Leftovers" ended,
which was such a wonderful show.

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:10.410
"Fargo" -- such a great season.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´re Emmy-nominated
for "Fargo."

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Congratulations for that.
-Thank you. Thank you!

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I have some questions
about those shows.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I´m always fascinated
by what people did

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
in their early life,
before they were actors.

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
You worked at a Best Buy.
-I did.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.925 size:81% position:41%
-In -- Near Cleveland.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Near Akron, yes.
-Near Akron. Of course.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:28.995
And that makes even more sense

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:31.231
because a young LeBron James
would come to the Best Buy.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, he did.
He would come all the time.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was so tall.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he would come
to my brother´s theater.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.671
He worked at a Regal Cinema.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was very personal
for us, always,

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:41.941
this LeBron James business,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because my brother
told my mother

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.912
that if LeBron left Cleveland

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.947
that he wasn´t going to propose
to his girlfriend.

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
-And so I was watching --

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.285
My parents were visiting me
in grad school or something,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:54.487 size:78% position:39%
and we were watching
"The Decision" on TV.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.656
And as soon as he said it,
my mom burst into tears.

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no.
-´Cause she was horrified.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.293
Now, my brother was just,
you know, buying some time.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.162
He didn´t really mean it.
She´s a fantastic woman.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:03.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re married.
They´re very happy.

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:04.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, good.
-Has a happy ending.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it does, also,
´cause LeBron came back.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that allowed
for their love to flourish.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, of course,
and we were happy to have him,

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:11.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause we really needed a win
in Cleveland.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.440
Let´s be clear about that.
-Good. I´m glad you got one.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hopefully you´ll bring
an Emmy back to Cleveland.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my gosh. I hope.
-Yeah, that would be great.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t think so.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.781
-You don´t think you´ll win or
you don´t think you´ll bring it

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.216
back to Cleveland if you do?

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, back to Akron.
I keep calling it Cleveland.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Touché. Touché.
They´re close enough.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:28.688
-I want to ask about this,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
because both
"The Leftovers" and "Fargo"

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.991
I would say had sort of --

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a bit of vagueness
to the endings,

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.329
which is very much in line
with what those shows are.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you have not --
In interviews, you have not

00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
gone out of your way
to try to explain to audiences

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you think,
as an actress, happened.

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was that a choice you made?
-Absolutely.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, A,
who cares what I think?

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.675
And I say that because --

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.511
You know, what´s important is
not the experience that I have.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s the experience
that you have.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:57.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wouldn´t want to
rob anybody of that moment

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
of sitting with
what happens in those shows

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
and thinking about for
themselves what they believe.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:03.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because what it does
is it reveals more about you

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.391 size:81% position:41%
than it does about me.

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:06.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had an acting teacher
that used to say --

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would always be crying
in scenes, you know?

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he´d be like,
"Carrie, dry it up.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it doesn´t matter
if you cry.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.633 size:81% position:41%
It matters if we cry."

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think
that´s absolutely right.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.836
-That´s great.
-So I´m just Captain Ambiguity.

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ll do all your
ambiguous endings.

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:21.508 size:75% position:38%
-And then, you know,
I have not been able

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:23.743 align:start size:94% position:6%
to stop thinking about the end
of "The Leftovers."

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
You obviously
played that character, Nora,

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a very long time --
three seasons.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now that you´ve been gone
from it for a while,

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you still feel a connection
with that character?

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:34.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, sure. I mean,
she taught me a lot about

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.289 size:88% position:44%
how to walk into a room.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she´s --

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:40.793
she´s much -- she´s much
less compromising than me.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was such a people-pleaser
in my 20s, you know?

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.633
And I think she just
didn´t put up with any of that.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:50.403
And it really changed the way
that I sort of stand and be.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.005
That´s fantastic.
What a gift to get from a role.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, absolutely, yeah.
-That´s fantastic.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.741
-That´s the best part of my job.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.877
-Another good part
of one of your acting roles is,

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.679
you met your husband in a play.
-I did.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Tracy Letts,
fantastic actor and writer.

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:04.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he´s pretty great.
-And you met him --

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
Though, you met him
on a production of

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Who´s Afraid
of Virginia Woolf,"

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.222 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is not where you think,
like, marriage is great.

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:10.857 size:88% position:44%
-No, it´s not usually --

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:12.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s not usually
an endorsement of marriage.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But, in fact,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think our production
was so successful because,

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, Pam McKinnon,
our director,

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.933
and then Tracy and Amy, who
were playing George and Martha,

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
they approached it
as a love story.

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.836
And I remember talking about it.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said,
"It´s a love story,"

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:26.739
and Tracy would always say,

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:28.841
"Wouldn´t you want your partner
to fight for you that hard?"

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:31.578
And that was such a beautiful
way of thinking about that play.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:33.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
That is definitely not --

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need to go back
and watch it again.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you should.
It still works.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.482 size:81% position:41%
It´s a very good play.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I´ve never been bored
ever watching it.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fantastic.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you and I
have something similar,

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I´ve told this story
on the show before.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
When I got married,
the day of our wedding,

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:47.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
my wife had food poisoning,
and we actually

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.095
had to go to the emergency room
in the morning.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
It all worked out.
But you had one --

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn´t even
get out of the hospital.

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, unfortunately.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.834 size:81% position:41%
You know, in Illinois,
when you get married,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have 60 days,
and then --

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What do you mean
you have 60 days?

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you have to register.
-Okay.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.739 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And if you don´t get married
in 60 days,

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to go
and pay and reregister,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
and nobody wants to do that.
-Right.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was day 59.

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:04.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was actually
doing "Gone Girl" in L.A.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.313
-So why did you wait so long?
Why´d you let it get to day 59?

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.815 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We´re actors.
We hardly see each other.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:10.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´ve been married four years.
It feels like 1 1/2.

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.555
-So, I came home the night
before it was gonna expire,

00:04:15.555 --> 00:04:17.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said,
"We have to go tomorrow."

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.292
And he said, "Yeah, yeah, yeah.
I´m not feeling very well."

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.693
We go to the emergency room,

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:23.496
he has emergency gallbladder
removal surgery on Saturday.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:26.132
So, by Sunday, our registration
was actually dead.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:27.300 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I came --

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
I brought our rings
and a little dress,

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:30.503
and I said, "Is there a chaplain
in the house?"

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was actually
talking to my mom,

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my little dress
was on the chair,

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was in Tracy´s T-shirt
and some grippy socks.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:37.910 size:84% position:42%
And she just walked in.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:40.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
She´s like, "Hello, I´m Robin.
I´m gonna do a wedding."

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "I got to go.
I´m getting married."

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:43.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.319 size:88% position:44%
And so, she just made up
this Lutheran ceremony.

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:47.553
It was just the three of us.

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my husband was so high.
-Oh, that´s great.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:52.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was so high.
-Was he -- Could he get up?

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:53.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
-No. So he was in bed?

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, in bed.
And his, like --

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:57.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
His gown was slightly
off the shoulder, you know?

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.698
He was just, like, so high.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He probably --

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
My dream was always
an off-the-shoulder gown.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife wouldn´t
let me do it, so...

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She was able --

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her gown probably fit
really easily.

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.409
-Yeah, she did really good.
She cleared out everything.

00:05:09.409 --> 00:05:10.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
She was ready to go.
-Good for her.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:11.911
That´s the way to do it.
-That´s the way to do it.

00:05:11.911 --> 00:05:13.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you don´t need
to go on a diet.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.515
Just get a little food poisoning
right at the end.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.917 size:84% position:42%
-Something. Absolutely.

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:19.652
-Well, and I think you have
an anniversary coming up?

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.087 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, end of the month.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:23.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always get the day mixed up,
because we actually cheated

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:25.024
by backdating it one day,
because it was expired.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think it´s the 30th.
-30th, right.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-State of Illinois,
it´s the 30th.

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:30.496
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.398
-I´ll make sure to send flowers
on that day.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.634
-Happy anniversary to you, too.
-Thank you very much.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
September 1st.

00:05:35.802 --> 00:05:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Carrie Coon, everybody!

